kers beyond surveillance for  instance prognosis monitoring the  severity  the tumour yeah so there you know there  are data that show for let's say for AFP  there are data that show that patients  with a high AFP often have higher rates  of recurrence after liver  transplantation resection or ablation so  and then you know there's a there's data  showing that patients who have elevated  very high elevations of AFP Pitka - or  AFP l3 have higher rates of vascular  invasion and or metastatic disease so  they are related to not only tumor  burden but - related to prognosis so in  similar to the gala score there's  actually another score called the  ballade score which incorporates these  three biomarkers and has been shown to  correlate with prognosis very well so I  think that there there is a potential  role for you know all three of these  biomarkers in terms of prognosis but I  think similar to where they are in  surveillance I think that really you  know more data is needed there but I  think that we're closer probably to  using actually them in prognosis than we  are in surveillance in my opinion I  would like to once again thank dr. Amit  Singhal for his presentation do you have  any final comments um I guess this is a  thing in general this is an exciting  time because I think for for many years  all we had was ultra sound and and AFP  and I think that the fact that these  particularly these two biomarkers are  getting closer to to having you know  high-quality data and getting closer to  the phase three validation I think it's  an exciting time because I think that we  really are now going to be able to  hopefully make strides in terms of  improving early detection for patients  that develop HCC great um I would also  like to thank our sponsor Abbott for  making it possible to bring this  presentation to you  this webinar has been approved for  continuing educational credits please  click on the CD button at the bottom  left corner and follow the process to  